{"term":"blackout","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:aae4739ddb2be6af57","definition":"A temporary loss of consciousness.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["blankout","faint","syncope"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["blackout bag","blackout bomb","blackout cake","blackout curtain","blackout date","blackout gag","blackout lamp","blackout poem","blackout poetry","blackouts","blackout skit","Brooklyn blackout cake","brownout","brown out","rolling blackout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blackout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:39468e0a1e543b0f73","definition":"A temporary loss of memory.","example":"“I mean, what is she even talking about? Got her pregnant at the Halloween party? What does that mean? I don't even remember that party. I was wasted.” “Yeah, me too. I browned out that evening.” “\"browned out\"? What's \"browned out\"?” “Oh, it's when you drink so much that everything goes brown. It's not as severe as a blackout, 'cause I remember bits and pieces. I like to call it \"browning out.\"”","pos":"noun","synonyms":["blankout"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["blackout bag","blackout bomb","blackout cake","blackout curtain","blackout date","blackout gag","blackout lamp","blackout poem","blackout poetry","blackouts","blackout skit","Brooklyn blackout cake","brownout","brown out","rolling blackout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blackout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5a63280f01a9b0952e","definition":"A large-scale power failure, and resulting loss of electricity to consumers.","example":"The repairs at the Koeberg Power Station in the Western Cape were on schedule for completion in the third week of May. This follows huge blackouts related to the problems at the power supplier since November.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["power cut","outage"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["blackout bag","blackout bomb","blackout cake","blackout curtain","blackout date","blackout gag","blackout lamp","blackout poem","blackout poetry","blackouts","blackout skit","Brooklyn blackout cake","brownout","brown out","rolling blackout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blackout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ce9b2e91fa019c87a3","definition":"An instance of censorship, especially a temporary one.","example":"media blackout","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["blackout bag","blackout bomb","blackout cake","blackout curtain","blackout date","blackout gag","blackout lamp","blackout poem","blackout poetry","blackouts","blackout skit","Brooklyn blackout cake","brownout","brown out","rolling blackout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blackout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:70924aaa72a93e0148","definition":"An intentional outage of a website or other online service, typically as a form of protest.","example":"the 2012 English Wikipedia blackout","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Internet","register":"Internet, countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["blackout bag","blackout bomb","blackout cake","blackout curtain","blackout date","blackout gag","blackout lamp","blackout poem","blackout poetry","blackouts","blackout skit","Brooklyn blackout cake","brownout","brown out","rolling blackout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blackout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:18803e9adc8a278b6e","definition":"The mandatory blocking of all light emanating from buildings, as well as outdoor and street lighting as a measure against aerial bombing or naval attack, as imposed during, e.g., World War II.","example":"In co-operation with the Government departments, the British railway companies prepared their stations, offices, docks, hotels, trains, and other premises for the necessary blackout of lighting that it was realised would be required in a state of emergency, and in the case of the experimental voluntary blackouts which took place in July and August the railway companies concerned co-operated in every way possible.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"historical","register":"countable, historical, uncountable","wordFamily":["blackout bag","blackout bomb","blackout cake","blackout curtain","blackout date","blackout gag","blackout lamp","blackout poem","blackout poetry","blackouts","blackout skit","Brooklyn blackout cake","brownout","brown out","rolling blackout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blackout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a443af1a8d76b2d223","definition":"The blocking out of as much light as possible.","example":"blackout blinds; blackout curtains","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"attributive","register":"attributive, countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["blackout bag","blackout bomb","blackout cake","blackout curtain","blackout date","blackout gag","blackout lamp","blackout poem","blackout poetry","blackouts","blackout skit","Brooklyn blackout cake","brownout","brown out","rolling blackout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blackout#Eng